00:00:02.790 --> 00:00:04.789 align:start position:0%
this masterpiece by famous catalan  architect anthony gowdy has been under  construction for nearly 140 years  although unfinished the sagrada familia  is one of barcelona's biggest  attractions  many people in barcelona thought they'd  never live to see it completed  but it might finally happen on the  centenary of gowdy's death in 2026  it's beautiful it still has to be  finished but once they finish it it will  be even more beautiful we'll be able to  admire the beauty of the whole complex  weather can be finished on time will  depend on tourists like these  gowdy demanded that the entire project  be funded from ticket sales and private  donations but constant shortfalls have  stole the project longer than perhaps  even he imagined  the pandemic brought construction to a  halt we didn't have visitors for almost  a year without receiving funds we had  very little but the construction board  decided to keep going ahead  but now the sagrada familia is facing a  new challenge  finishing the main entrance will require  demolishing several nearby buildings  thousands of people could be evicted and  many don't want to move  our proposal both for the city hall and  the board of construction is that we are  very comfortable in our homes  we've paid for them and they are totally  legally ours  balancing the rights of residents  against a major architectural spectacle  for the city has put local authorities  in a difficult position  there aren't magical solutions here we  don't think that in order to finish the  basilica all buildings involved must be  demolished but we also think it isn't  likely that all buildings will be saved  we must see the different options and we  as local government with the neighbors  and the sagrada familia are working on  that  the project has been delayed many times  by the spanish civil war in the 1930s by  economic downturns and most recently by  the pandemic  gowdy died in 1926 and never expected  the sagrada familia to be finished in  his lifetime  referring to who he described as god he  was often known to say  my client is in no rush  vincent monaghan al jazeera
 

